#: ../../source/outgoing/api_responses.rst:258
msgid "Pagination Responses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/api_responses.rst:260
msgid ""
"When returning paginated results from an API endpoint, you can use the "
"``paginate()`` method to return the results along with the pagination "
"information. This helps to keep consistent responses across your API, "
"while providing all of the information that clients will need to properly"
" page through the results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/api_responses.rst:266
msgid "Example Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/api_responses.rst:270
msgid "A typical response might look like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/api_responses.rst:302
msgid ""
"The ``paginate()`` method will always wrap the results in a ``data`` "
"element, and will also include ``meta`` and ``links`` elements to help "
"the client page through the results. If there are no results, the "
"``data`` element will be an empty array, and the ``meta`` and ``links`` "
"elements will still be present, but with values that indicate no results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/api_responses.rst:306
msgid ""
"You can also pass it a Builder instance instead of a Model, as long as "
"the Builder is properly configured with the table name and any necessary "
"joins or where clauses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/api_responses.rst:317
msgid "The resource to paginate, either a Model or a Builder instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/api_responses.rst:318
msgid "The number of items to return per page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/api_responses.rst:319
msgid "Optional transformer class name to transform the results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/api_responses.rst:321
msgid ""
"Generates a paginated response from the given resource. The resource can "
"be either a Model or a Builder instance. The method will automatically "
"determine the current page from the request's query parameters. The "
"response will include the paginated data, along with metadata about the "
"pagination state and links to navigate through the pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/api_responses.rst:326
msgid ""
"If you provide a ``$transformWith`` parameter with a transformer class "
"name, each item in the paginated results will be transformed using that "
"transformer before being returned. This is useful for controlling the "
"structure and content of your API responses. See :ref:`API Transformers "
"<api_transformers>` for more information on creating and using "
"transformers."
msgstr ""

